1
00:00:06,804 --> 00:00:10,967
Seven sections. Twenty-nine
parts. One thread.

2
00:00:11,047 --> 00:00:13,454
Nothing appears with a nature of its own.

3
00:00:13,534 --> 00:00:15,524
And what appears still works.

4
00:00:16,336 --> 00:00:18,964
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

5
00:00:19,044 --> 00:00:22,922
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

6
00:00:23,732 --> 00:00:27,162
If you think you understand
dependent arising, you don't.

7
00:00:27,242 --> 00:00:30,056
I can agree that nothing
has an essence of its own,

8
00:00:30,136 --> 00:00:36,136
say so fluently, and still hold the world
exactly as before. Solid. Out there.

9
00:00:36,304 --> 00:00:39,204
Mine. Agreeing is not living in it.

10
00:00:40,008 --> 00:00:42,582
So the series does not argue first.

11
00:00:42,662 --> 00:00:46,508
The early sections set two
ways of seeing side by side.

12
00:00:46,588 --> 00:00:48,791
One takes things to stand on their own.

13
00:00:48,871 --> 00:00:50,585
The other looks at how they form.

14
00:00:50,665 --> 00:00:52,568
Then they ask which one holds.

15
00:00:52,648 --> 00:00:56,427
By experience, by logic,
and by how things work.

16
00:00:56,507 --> 00:00:59,579
The later sections take up
the logic, the tradition,

17
00:00:59,659 --> 00:01:02,464
Nāgārjuna, and the hardest questions.

18
00:01:03,268 --> 00:01:05,770
This overview says what each section asks,

19
00:01:05,850 --> 00:01:07,703
and what runs through all of them.

20
00:01:08,504 --> 00:01:10,100
First, the thread.

21
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:12,686
It has two halves, and both matter.

22
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:15,911
Nothing appears with a nature of its own.

23
00:01:15,991 --> 00:01:20,721
Look for the apple apart from seeing,
touching and tasting, and it is not found.

24
00:01:20,801 --> 00:01:24,511
Look for the sound apart from the
bell, the air and the hearing.

25
00:01:24,591 --> 00:01:26,916
Look for the one who ages and dies.

26
00:01:26,996 --> 00:01:30,399
Each time, what is looked
for is not there by itself.

27
00:01:31,192 --> 00:01:33,100
And what appears still works.

28
00:01:33,180 --> 00:01:34,961
The apple is still bitten.

29
00:01:35,041 --> 00:01:36,592
The bell still rings.

30
00:01:36,672 --> 00:01:41,198
A car still knocks you down, and the
grief of a family is not an illusion.

31
00:01:41,278 --> 00:01:42,951
Nothing is taken away.

32
00:01:43,031 --> 00:01:47,235
What goes is only the extra weight of
taking things to stand on their own.

33
00:01:48,044 --> 00:01:51,415
Drop the first half, and
the world stays solid,

34
00:01:51,495 --> 00:01:53,023
out there, mine.

35
00:01:53,103 --> 00:01:56,229
Drop the second, and
emptiness turns ghostly,

36
00:01:56,309 --> 00:01:57,887
a void behind things.

37
00:01:57,967 --> 00:02:00,812
The series keeps both, in every section.

38
00:02:01,608 --> 00:02:04,816
Section 1 asks: is the
world already there,

39
00:02:04,896 --> 00:02:08,330
finished, waiting to be
seen? Or is it formed?

40
00:02:09,124 --> 00:02:10,679
It starts with an apple.

41
00:02:10,759 --> 00:02:12,826
Nothing seems more plainly there.

42
00:02:12,906 --> 00:02:15,040
Then it looks at how the apple forms.

43
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:19,510
Sight, sound, smell,
taste, touch and mind,

44
00:02:19,590 --> 00:02:22,042
meeting, and named apple in the meeting.

45
00:02:22,856 --> 00:02:25,009
Next, one bowl of liquid.

46
00:02:25,089 --> 00:02:26,680
A human sees water.

47
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:28,731
A hungry ghost sees pus.

48
00:02:28,811 --> 00:02:32,006
A fish meets its home. A god meets nectar.

49
00:02:32,086 --> 00:02:35,448
No finished world waits
underneath, seen differently.

50
00:02:36,252 --> 00:02:40,415
Then two physicists, where they echo
this, and where I part from them.

51
00:02:40,495 --> 00:02:42,481
And last, the conclusion.

52
00:02:42,561 --> 00:02:48,260
Without essence, nothing turns ghostly.
It still rains. You still get sick.

53
00:02:49,072 --> 00:02:53,181
Section 2 asks: given all
this, what is it that appears?

54
00:02:53,996 --> 00:02:56,842
A sound, a colour, a thought.

55
00:02:56,922 --> 00:03:01,380
Each is vivid, not found, and
dependently arisen, all at once.

56
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:05,456
Then the habit retreats and looks
for a floor. The real instant.

57
00:03:05,536 --> 00:03:09,722
The smallest piece. Space
itself. None is found.

58
00:03:09,802 --> 00:03:14,151
The solid, the dreamlike and the
described are set side by side,

59
00:03:14,231 --> 00:03:15,918
and none of them is the floor.

60
00:03:15,998 --> 00:03:18,055
Not even the web of conditions.

61
00:03:18,864 --> 00:03:23,218
Then clarity. Is there a knower
behind it? No layer is found.

62
00:03:23,298 --> 00:03:26,180
Nothing stands between
the hearing and the sound.

63
00:03:26,260 --> 00:03:28,453
The clarity is the sound itself.

64
00:03:29,260 --> 00:03:33,668
From there, how what is seen can be
complete, and yet wholly dependent.

65
00:03:33,748 --> 00:03:37,921
Three parts follow Dōgen's
images: the shore and the boat,

66
00:03:38,001 --> 00:03:40,991
firewood and ash, the fish and the bird.

67
00:03:41,071 --> 00:03:44,239
One part goes to Huayan,
with its net of jewels,

68
00:03:44,319 --> 00:03:45,964
and says where I keep a guard.

69
00:03:46,044 --> 00:03:49,252
And the last part shows where
the big ideas come from.

70
00:03:49,332 --> 00:03:54,225
Privacy, objectivity, causal
power, inside and outside.

71
00:03:54,305 --> 00:03:58,047
Each is a real feature of
appearing, misread as a thing.

72
00:03:58,856 --> 00:04:03,002
Section 3 asks: once neither
mind nor matter is the floor,

73
00:04:03,082 --> 00:04:05,098
is either worth leaning towards?

74
00:04:05,916 --> 00:04:08,979
Hear the rain and ask, what is it, really?

75
00:04:09,059 --> 00:04:10,718
The question looks innocent.

76
00:04:10,798 --> 00:04:12,797
It already carries a worldview.

77
00:04:12,877 --> 00:04:14,903
There has to be something underneath.

78
00:04:14,983 --> 00:04:18,087
Mind, or matter, or some third stuff.

79
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:22,772
Then the place this habit is felt
most sharply: the Hard Problem.

80
00:04:22,852 --> 00:04:26,264
How does grey matter give rise
to the felt redness of red?

81
00:04:26,344 --> 00:04:29,538
Seen through emptiness, the
question is not answered.

82
00:04:29,618 --> 00:04:31,730
What it stands on is not found.

83
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:34,706
And last, the living fact.

84
00:04:34,786 --> 00:04:38,320
Divide mind from matter, and
the gap cannot be bridged.

85
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:41,545
Reach for a cup, and
no gap is ever crossed.

86
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:47,294
Section 4 asks: how do we reason, once
nothing is taken to have a nature of its

87
00:04:47,374 --> 00:04:48,574
own?

88
00:04:48,844 --> 00:04:52,505
Watch a candle burn, and the
answer comes before any thought.

89
00:04:52,585 --> 00:04:54,135
The flame is changing.

90
00:04:54,215 --> 00:04:57,070
Something is there, and
something is happening to it.

91
00:04:57,150 --> 00:04:59,366
That answer is a whole way of reasoning.

92
00:04:59,446 --> 00:05:02,006
First a thing, then what happens to it.

93
00:05:02,816 --> 00:05:05,186
The other way starts a step earlier.

94
00:05:05,266 --> 00:05:08,791
It asks how anything comes to
be picked out as a thing at all.

95
00:05:09,588 --> 00:05:14,390
Then the questions we ask about anything.
When did it start? Where did it go?

96
00:05:14,470 --> 00:05:17,610
Is it the same one? Each
asks where a thing is.

97
00:05:17,690 --> 00:05:21,156
When no thing is found, the
questions lose their object.

98
00:05:21,236 --> 00:05:24,132
And the conventional is
not merely conventional.

99
00:05:24,212 --> 00:05:25,862
It is where truth lives.

100
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:29,254
Last, continuity without a carrier.

101
00:05:29,334 --> 00:05:32,664
Not a passenger, but a
melody you know by heart.

102
00:05:32,744 --> 00:05:35,318
The path becomes arranging conditions.

103
00:05:36,116 --> 00:05:40,343
Section 5 asks: how does the
tradition teach dependent arising,

104
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:42,114
and who goes round the wheel?

105
00:05:42,912 --> 00:05:44,630
Here I stay with the tradition.

106
00:05:44,710 --> 00:05:46,464
When this is, that is.

107
00:05:46,544 --> 00:05:49,494
The twelve links, forward and in reverse.

108
00:05:49,574 --> 00:05:51,790
The chain is reeds leaning on each other,

109
00:05:51,870 --> 00:05:53,602
not a line of dominoes.

110
00:05:54,412 --> 00:05:56,497
Then, who ages and dies?

111
00:05:56,577 --> 00:05:58,969
Not a valid question, the Buddha says.

112
00:05:59,049 --> 00:06:03,018
Karma and rebirth are kept, with
no one in them who goes round.

113
00:06:03,098 --> 00:06:07,126
That removes one objection to
rebirth. It does not prove it.

114
00:06:07,928 --> 00:06:10,176
Last, where the chain is cut.

115
00:06:10,256 --> 00:06:11,847
The pain still comes.

116
00:06:11,927 --> 00:06:14,863
What ends is the second
arrow, what I add to it.

117
00:06:14,943 --> 00:06:18,441
And ignorance ends by seeing,
not by stopping thought.

118
00:06:19,236 --> 00:06:23,522
Section 6 asks: how does
Nāgārjuna read the same teaching?

119
00:06:24,328 --> 00:06:27,251
He bows to the Buddha for
teaching dependent arising,

120
00:06:27,331 --> 00:06:29,592
without ceasing, without arising.

121
00:06:29,672 --> 00:06:31,983
How can arising be without arising?

122
00:06:32,063 --> 00:06:35,163
The answer is how he reads
when this is, that is.

123
00:06:35,243 --> 00:06:37,518
A pattern, not a handover.

124
00:06:38,324 --> 00:06:42,470
Then his chapter on the twelve links,
the one chapter of his Middle Way with no

125
00:06:42,550 --> 00:06:46,835
refutation in it. Karma,
rebirth and the path are kept.

126
00:06:46,915 --> 00:06:48,891
Only the owner is left out.

127
00:06:49,704 --> 00:06:51,761
Last, how the chain ends.

128
00:06:51,841 --> 00:06:54,044
Ignorance is not a thing to destroy.

129
00:06:54,124 --> 00:06:57,060
It is a way of taking things: elaboration.

130
00:06:57,140 --> 00:06:59,701
And elaboration stops in emptiness.

131
00:07:00,508 --> 00:07:03,933
Section 7 asks: what does
this view do for others,

132
00:07:04,013 --> 00:07:06,805
and does it survive its
strongest objections?

133
00:07:07,616 --> 00:07:09,279
First, compassion.

134
00:07:09,359 --> 00:07:12,731
Emptiness does not cause it,
and does not diminish it.

135
00:07:12,811 --> 00:07:15,679
As I see it, compassion has two sides.

136
00:07:15,759 --> 00:07:20,638
An open heart, which shows itself as
the habit of standing apart loosens.

137
00:07:20,718 --> 00:07:23,754
And a learning, which
grows as it is practised.

138
00:07:24,564 --> 00:07:30,426
Then six objections, put as fairly as I
can. Is this nihilism? Is it all mind?

139
00:07:30,506 --> 00:07:33,469
Is it only concepts, so anything goes?

140
00:07:33,549 --> 00:07:37,722
Is dissolving the Hard Problem just
avoiding it? Is the physics stretched?

141
00:07:37,802 --> 00:07:41,205
Is emptiness, or the
web, the new absolute?

142
00:07:42,016 --> 00:07:44,821
How to read it. In order, if you can.

143
00:07:44,901 --> 00:07:47,334
Each section leans on the ones before.

144
00:07:47,414 --> 00:07:51,016
The conventional of Section
4 is used in Section 7.

145
00:07:51,096 --> 00:07:55,396
The seamless interaction of
Section 3 comes back in compassion.

146
00:07:56,204 --> 00:07:58,031
Or start where your question is.

147
00:07:58,111 --> 00:08:00,001
Each part can be read alone.

148
00:08:00,081 --> 00:08:03,764
If your question is mind and
matter, start at Section 3.

149
00:08:03,844 --> 00:08:07,328
If it is karma and rebirth,
start at Section 5.

150
00:08:08,136 --> 00:08:13,400
And try the tests. Every part has small
tests, to be tried in ordinary moments.

151
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:16,566
They are gathered in one
place, in the practice guide.

152
00:08:16,646 --> 00:08:18,948
Because agreeing is not living in it.

153
00:08:19,756 --> 00:08:23,240
This is the overview of the
Dependent Arising series.

154
00:08:24,056 --> 00:08:26,467
Nothing appears with a nature of its own.

155
00:08:26,547 --> 00:08:28,278
And the bell still rings.

